cket; statuses remain provisional. Overflow records are explicit and require their source pointers.","readiness":{"blockers":"NO_CLAUSE_INVENTORY|FIRST_END_UNPROVED|SAVINGS_RESIDUALS_NOT_CLOSED|LATER_SOURCE_SEARCH_NOT_RECORDED|OPUS_MEDIA_REFETCH_NEEDED","claim_present":"no","claim_record_errors":"","decision_origin":"opus_complete_addition","exhausted_steps":"","instrument_id":"EO:11313","provisional_status":"no","ready_for_human_review":"no","ready_tier":"","step_clause_inventory":"open","step_counterevidence":"open","step_ending_or_current_basis":"open","step_opus_media":"open","step_original_text":"done","step_provisional_status":"done","step_savings_residuals":"open","step_shared_sources":"n/a","steps_applicable":"7","steps_done":"2"},"readiness_blockers":[{"step":"ending_or_current_basis","what":"provisional NO, but no job found a whole-order-end candidate"}],"schema":"eo-case-bundle/v1","status":"no","text_pointers":[{"first_1500_characters":"Executive Order 11313\nPROVIDING THAT CERTAIN OFFICERS MAY ACT AS  \nPOSTMASTER GENERAL\nBy virtue of the authority vested in me by Section 3347 of Title 5 of \nthe United States Code and Section 301 of Title 3 of the United \nStates Code, and as President of the United States, it is ordered as \nfollows:\nS ection  1. In  the event of a vacancy in the office of Postmaster \nGeneral or during the absence or disability of the Postmaster General, \nthe Deputy Postmaster General shall act as Postmaster General.\nS ec. 2. During any period when, by reason of absence, disability, \nor vacancy in office, neither the Postmaster General nor the Deputy \nPostmaster General is available to exercise the powers or perform the \nduties of the office of Postmaster General, an Assistant Postmaster \nGeneral or the General Counsel of the Post Office Department, in such \norder as the Postmaster General may from time to time prescribe in \nwriting, shall act as Postmaster General. I f  no such order of succes­\nsion is in effect at that time, they shall act as Postmaster General in \nthe order in which they shall have taken office as Assistant Postmasters \nGeneral or General Counsel.\nS ec. 3. The fo llo w in g  are hereby superseded:\n(1) Executive Order No. 10154 of August 22,1950.\n(2) Executive Order No. 10558 of September 8,1954.\n(3) Executive Order No. 10686 of November 1,1956.\nT h e W h it e H ouse ,\nOctober 15 ,  1966.\nL yndon  B. J ohnson\n[F.R. Doc. 66-11383; Filed, Oct. 17,' 1966; 10:26 a.m.]","path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/texts/cd-job-fr-originals-11313-28c731eac5.txt","sha256":"92ee6e4c8311ca199a62b9cefaf4eca24c6d80c477a3dc8475de91151cd3e9a3","source":{"line":2291,"path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"aeddabdf417a9d70b995cbced4de02afdef0313d6d7a4d5a5ce13970ba295fda"}},{"first_1500_characters":"Instrument: EO:11313\nSource: https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1966-10-18/pdf/FR-1966-10-18.pdf\nSHA-256 of the downloaded file: 28c731eac574fbd684f7ed7d0218339b7925b1debdfd1b463b007f8dceb42a6f\nLocation: 31 FR 13417, PDF pages 9-9 (confidence high)\nMachine-extracted text layer of the official PDF (OCR for 1936-1994 scans). May contain recognition errors and parts of neighbouring documents on the same pages. Not an authenticated transcription: check the PDF pages.\n\n=== PDF page 9 of 52 ===\nTHE PRESIDENT 13417\nExecutive Order 11313\nPROVIDING THAT CERTAIN OFFICERS MAY ACT AS  \nPOSTMASTER GENERAL\nBy virtue of the authority vested in me by Section 3347 of Title 5 of \nthe United States Code and Section 301 of Title 3 of the United \nStates Code, and as President of the United States, it is ordered as \nfollows:\nS ection  1. In  the event of a vacancy in the office of Postmaster \nGeneral or during the absence or disability of the Postmaster General, \nthe Deputy Postmaster General shall act as Postmaster General.\nS ec. 2. During any period when, by reason of absence, disability, \nor vacancy in office, neither the Postmaster General nor the Deputy \nPostmaster General is available to exercise the powers or perform the \nduties of the office of Postmaster General, an Assistant Postmaster \nGeneral or the General Counsel of the Post Office Department, in such \norder as the Postmaster General may from time to time prescribe in \nwriting, shall act as Postmaster General. I f  no such order ","path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/texts/EO_11313.txt","sha256":"1e2f995717f54b1e7bafabd2ebd43d7205f9f0da69d060176a66596cf02acfd4","source":{"line":1198,"path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"1e77014eafbf3ae3eb3f61746cd56347a250ded1418e8e57ff86dbc571ae6e71"}}]}
